   "html_text": "If what an agent ought to do does depend on her moral beliefs, then we face the question of how agents should act when they are morally uncertain. One simple proposal, which Lockhart (2000) dubs “My Favorite Theory” (MFT), is that she should simply follow the moral theory in which she has greatest credence, disregarding all other moral theories. This view has been defended by Gracely (1996) and Gustafsson and Torpman (2014). But it faces substantial difficulties. First, it simply seems intuitive",
